│ Okay, let’s address this. The core issue is  │
│ that display_for_field was incorrectly       │
│ calling json.dumps to render JSONField       │
│ values in the Django admin, resulting in     │
│ invalid JSON being displayed. The fix is to  │
│ use prepare_value instead, which handles the │
│ necessary formatting for display.            │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The display_for_field function currently     │
│ uses json.dumps to serialize the value of a  │
│ JSONField. This produces a JSON string,      │
│ which is not what we want to display in the  │
│ admin. Instead, we need to call              │
│ JSONField.prepare_value to get a string      │
│ representation suitable for display. This    │
│ method handles the formatting and ensures    │
│ that the output is valid and readable in the │
│ admin interface.                             │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]/django/contrib/admin/utils.py[/file  │
│  [original] def display_for_field(request,   │
